Are you a highly motivated System Integrator fluent in German? EUROPEAN DYNAMICS is seeking a skilled System Integrator to join our dynamic team driving complex enterprise projects.
What You'll Do:

• Set-up, further development and maintenance of the development as well as build and deployment architecture;

• Regular performance of software builds with adaptations, extensions and implementation of corresponding automation for the software builds and structures;

• Regular performance of software installations on the various development and test environments as well as on the production environment;

• Performance of software installations and application of updates;

• Coordination and performance of the quality assurance of builds and deployments;

• Maintenance of the code repositories and performance of release branchings;

• Functional and technical production monitoring of the application;

• Anticipation and early identification of problems;

• Derivation, formulation and implementation of problem-solving strategies;

• Target-group-appropriate communication and explanation of problems and their effects to the Client;

• Implementation of suitable measures taking into account functional and non-functional requirements (e.g. high availability of the system) as well as extensive quality assurance;

• Assumption of production responsibility;
Requirements

• In-depth knowledge of distributed systems with a large number of components;

• In-depth knowledge of the application of build and deployment automation (e.g. Gitlab, Jenkins);

• In-depth knowledge of configuration management tools (Puppet, Ansible);

• In-depth knowledge of version control systems and of dependency - management, with Maven and NPM or equivalent technologies;

• In-depth knowledge of setting up CI/CD pipelines for Java and JavaScript / TypeScript - components;

• In-depth knowledge of cloud technologies, in particular in configuration management, with software containers and their orchestration as well as the setting up of CI/CD - pipelines using containers;

• In-depth knowledge in the field of DevSecOps;

• In-depth knowledge of the set-up and handling of distributed systems (incl. geo-redundancy);

• At least 3 years of demonstrable practical experience;

• Based in Germany;

• Fluent command of oral and written German (level C2 required) and English at a sufficient level;

Benefits
We believe in rewarding talent and dedication. Here's what you can expect as part of our team:

• Competitive full-time salary;

• Private Health Coverage on the Company’s group program;

• Flexible Working Hours;

• Top-of-the-Line Tools;

• Professional Development: Benefit from language courses, specialized training, and continuous learning opportunities;

• Career Growth: Work with some of the most innovative and exciting specialists in the industry;

• Dynamic Work Environment: Thrive in a setting that offers challenging goals, autonomy, and mentoring, fostering both personal and company growth.

If you want an exciting challenge, work with some of the coolest technologies, and enjoy your time doing it, then join us! Submit your detailed CV in English, quoting reference: ( SI/11/26 ).
You may also consider all our other open vacancies by visiting the career section of our website () and follow us on Twitter (@EURODYN_Careers) and LinkedIn.
